{:edb/db-before-t 1974 :edb/db-after-t 1975 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535287 50 #inst "2026-10-08T21:16:55.861Z" 13194139535287 true] [17592186068644 1020 #edb/ref 17592186341777 13194139535287 true] [17592186068644 1020 #edb/ref 17592186341784 13194139535287 true] [17592186068676 1020 #edb/ref 17592186341791 13194139535287 true] [17592186068676 1020 #edb/ref 17592186341798 13194139535287 true] [17592186068676 1020 #edb/ref 17592186341805 13194139535287 true] [17592186341777 1017 #edb/ref 17592186341778 13194139535287 true] [17592186341777 1089 "q-11357" 13194139535287 true] [17592186341777 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535287 true] [17592186341777 1100 "Evaluate $\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+2x+17}{({x}^{2}+7)(x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139535287 true] [17592186341777 1113 #uuid "9debd0df-2771-5276-9781-4c4c107557fd" 13194139535287 true] [17592186341777 1145 "The quadratic factor ${x}^{2}+7$ is irreducible, so we proceed with the following partial fraction decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}+2x+17}{({x}^{2}+7)(x+1)} & =\\frac{Ax+B}{{x}^{2}+7}+\\frac{C}{x+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $({x}^{2}+7)(x+1),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2x+17 & =(Ax+B)(x+1)+C({x}^{2}+7).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for the unknown constants using the usual methods, we get $A=-1,B=3,$ and $C=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+2x+17}{({x}^{2}+7)(x+1)}=\\frac{-x+3}{{x}^{2}+7}+\\frac{2}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nWe now integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+2x+17}{({x}^{2}+7)(x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{-x+3}{{x}^{2}+7}+\\frac{2}{x+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\int \\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+7}\\,\\text{d}x+3\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+7}\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we use a substitution $u={x}^{2}+7.$ Then $\\text{d}u=2x\\,\\text{d}x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+7}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{u})\\frac{\\text{d}u}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+7| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+7).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second integral, we use the fact that $\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{a}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{a}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{a}),$ which results in\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+7}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{7}}).\n$$\n\nFinally, for the third integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|.\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+2x+17}{({x}^{2}+7)(x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+7}\\,\\text{d}x+3\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+7}\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+7)+3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{7}})+2\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+K \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+7)+\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{7}}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{7}})+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+K\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535287 true] [17592186341778 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341779 13194139535287 true] [17592186341778 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341780 13194139535287 true] [17592186341778 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341781 13194139535287 true] [17592186341778 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341782 13194139535287 true] [17592186341778 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341783 13194139535287 true] [17592186341778 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535287 true] [17592186341778 1041 "selection" 13194139535287 true] [17592186341778 1104 #edb/ref 17592186341783 13194139535287 true] [17592186341778 1110 #uuid "e3bfb3e0-02eb-584b-b143-02af187f4a8d" 13194139535287 true] [17592186341779 1034 "-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+7)+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{7}}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\s