x+4}{{x}^{2}+4x-6}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{u})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4x-6|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4{x}^{2}+12x-12}{x({x}^{2}+4x-6)}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{2x+4}{{x}^{2}+4x-6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4x-6|+K.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535287 true] [17592186341792 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341793 13194139535287 true] [17592186341792 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341794 13194139535287 true] [17592186341792 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341795 13194139535287 true] [17592186341792 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341796 13194139535287 true] [17592186341792 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341797 13194139535287 true] [17592186341792 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535287 true] [17592186341792 1041 "selection" 13194139535287 true] [17592186341792 1104 #edb/ref 17592186341795 13194139535287 true] [17592186341792 1110 #uuid "75d6192b-2fda-552b-b654-d948c73582f0" 13194139535287 true] [17592186341793 1034 "\\frac{2}{x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4x-6|+K" 13194139535287 true] [17592186341793 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535287 true] [17592186341793 1111 #uuid "63df8e8a-de87-5f04-94ba-1adeaa275a29" 13194139535287 true] [17592186341794 1034 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4x-6|+K" 13194139535287 true] [17592186341794 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535287 true] [17592186341794 1111 #uuid "2026753c-2a95-516a-8e36-a8b45a756c70" 13194139535287 true] [17592186341795 1034 "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4x-6|+K" 13194139535287 true] [17592186341795 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535287 true] [17592186341795 1111 #uuid "68de0c6b-840f-50fe-8dfa-9a0944c1edb0" 13194139535287 true] [17592186341796 1034 "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4x-6|}+K" 13194139535287 true] [17592186341796 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535287 true] [17592186341796 1111 #uuid "367e2e6e-aa98-522f-8acb-9b4997e4dbe8" 13194139535287 true] [17592186341797 1034 "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4x-6|+K" 13194139535287 true] [17592186341797 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535287 true] [17592186341797 1111 #uuid "f320924a-a119-5145-bb90-6cd098e55ba0" 13194139535287 true] [17592186341798 1017 #edb/ref 17592186341799 13194139535287 true] [17592186341798 1089 "q-3615" 13194139535287 true] [17592186341798 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535287 true] [17592186341798 1100 "Evaluate $\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+x-3}{({x}^{2}-2x+3)(x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139535287 true] [17592186341798 1113 #uuid "bb88ac70-729c-5c15-8fad-c3a30aa15d49" 13194139535287 true] [17592186341798 1145 "Notice that the quadratic factor in the denominator has a negative discriminant:\n\n$$\nD=(-2)^{2}-4(1)(3)=-8<0\n$$\n\nSo, we proceed with the following partial fraction decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}+x-3}{({x}^{2}-2x+3)(x+1)} & =\\frac{Ax+B}{{x}^{2}-2x+3}+\\frac{C}{x+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,$ $B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $({x}^{2}-2x+3)(x+1)$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+x-3 & =(Ax+B)(x+1)+C({x}^{2}-2x+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for the unknown constants using the usual methods, we get  $A=\\frac{3}{2},$ $B=-\\frac{3}{2},$ and $C=-\\frac{1}{2}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+x-3}{({x}^{2}-2x+3)(x+1)}=\\frac{3x-3}{2({x}^{2}-2x+3)}-\\frac{1}{2(x+1)}.\n$$\n\nNow we integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration only at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+x-3}{({x}^{2}-2x+3)(x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{3x-3}{2({x}^{2}-2x+3)}-\\frac{1}{2(x+1)})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\int \\frac{x-1}{{x}^{2}-2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we use the substitution $u={x}^{2}-2x+3.$ Then $(2x-2)\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x-1}{{x}^{2}-2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{u})\\frac{\\text{d}u}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}-2x+3| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-2x+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second integral we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+x-3}{({x}^{2}-2x+3)(x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3}{2}\\int \\frac{x-1}{{x}^{2}-2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-2x+3)-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+K \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-2x+3)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+K.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535287 true] [17592186341799 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341800 13194139535287 true] [17592186341799 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341801 13194139535287 true] [17592186341799 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341802 13194139535287 true] [17592186341799 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341803 13194139535287 true] [17592186341799 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341804 13194139535287 true] [17592186341799 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535287 true] [17592186341799 1041 "selection" 13194139535287 true] [17592186341799 1104 #edb/ref 17592186341801 13194139535287 true] [17592186341799 1110 #uuid "aace1bc0-4029-56bd-83f2-c490e8c58495" 13194139535287 true] [17592186341800 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-2x+3)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+K" 13194139535287 true] [17592186341800 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535287 true] [17592186341800 1111 #uuid "0b3faeb1-f4ef-52b9-89c6-69902cf18d33" 13194139535287 true] [17592186341801 1034 "\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-2x+3)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+K" 13194139535287 true] [17592186341